{"questions":[{"question_id":"L8DAsDIqZymtx3Us","paperTitle":"JEE Advanced 2014 Paper 2 Offline","year":2014,"examDate":2014,"subject":"physics","chapter":"work-power-and-energy","chapterGroup":"mechanics","topic":"energy","type":"mcq","marks":3,"negMarks":1,"permalink":"a-tennis-ball-is-dropped-on-a-horizontal-smooth-surface-it-2014-marks-3-l8dasdiqzymtx3us.htm","content":"A tennis ball is dropped on a horizontal smooth surface. It bounces back to its original position after hitting the surface. The force on the ball during the collision is proportional to the length of compression of the ball. Which one of the following sketches describes the variation of its kinetic energy K with time t most appropriately? The figures are only illustrative and not to the scale.","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"<img class=\"question-image\" src=\"https://gateclass.cdn.examgoal.net/GTHVNE47ANgzXpqX7/fENtzY0dsUWkV07kfzw8KEDjLrj8N/soRF173aL3JcycLabHCFlP/uploadfile.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"JEE Advanced 2014 Paper 2 Offline Physics - Work Power &amp; Energy Question 29 English Option 1\">"},{"identifier":"B","content":"<img class=\"question-image\" src=\"https://gateclass.cdn.examgoal.net/5B90U4XaTfUMlm09P/chsy0hGnnYE8kqcUYPMve0ifvveBk/2rD4TrolGfcFHpCPDzXnDX/uploadfile.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"JEE Advanced 2014 Paper 2 Offline Physics - Work Power &amp; Energy Question 29 English Option 2\">"},{"identifier":"C","content":"<img class=\"question-image\" src=\"https://gateclass.cdn.examgoal.net/7FgYsJEXneWufxJGs/Qso2es97NInRtoKx5mLyeRRJuy3mp/No4O8rT8ONHRcuqOdOhiAz/uploadfile.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"JEE Advanced 2014 Paper 2 Offline Physics - Work Power &amp; Energy Question 29 English Option 3\">"},{"identifier":"D","content":"<img class=\"question-image\" src=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/vT5PeDIte9InZnlpi/gzJR1kDIBywH08RGqANmUX6EuIAyY/XHkeRzRiA7i1ocLUrr6GCS/uploadfile.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"JEE Advanced 2014 Paper 2 Offline Physics - Work Power &amp; Energy Question 29 English Option 4\">"}],"correct_options":["B"],"explanation":"<p>As tennis ball is dropped, so its initial velocity, u = 0</p>\n<p>Suppose its velocity at any time t = v</p>\n<p>Acceleration due to gravity = g</p>\n<p><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.186ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.509ex\" height=\"1.251ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -471 667 553\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2234\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2234\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> v = u + gt</p>\n<p><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.054ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2.262ex\" height=\"1.242ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -525 1000 549\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"21D2\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-21D2\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> v = gt ..... (i)</p>\n<p>We know, kinetic energy,</p>\n<p><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.781ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"23.446ex\" height=\"2.737ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -864.9 10363 1209.9\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D43E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D43E\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1166.8,0)\"><use data-c=\"3D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-3D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXA